     I suggest that you re-read NetHack's license.  If you provide binaries
to someone, you must also be prepared to give them the sources.  NetHack is
not in the public domain; there are specific terms and conditions imposed
on its distribution.  (Basically it's free, but any recipient must receive
the same freedom as you had, including the opportunity to make local
modifications to the sources, bound by the same license.)  I think that
offering to provide the changes needed to convert the "official" version
into your modified version is enough to comply in a case like this.

